From 1774aae9fd9f33e730fa305522ec63397b2ce58e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lyqed <antondoeswonders@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:04:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] vertex: operator-configured billing labels for invoice-grade
 attribution

The native Vertex generateContent path (#2023) shipped native Gemini
requests and a top-level `labels` field, but that field is caller
pass-through: the label values on the request come from the client, so
the operator cannot decide how Vertex spend is attributed. A caller can
omit labels or send another team's value, and the value that reaches
Google Cloud billing is caller-asserted rather than operator-set.

This adds an operator-set `labels` field to the Vertex provider config
so the value reaching Google Cloud billing is operator-decided. Each
label is either a static `value` or a CEL `expression` evaluated against
the request, following the AWS STS session tag pattern already used for
Bedrock cost attribution (#2435/#2447).

Operator labels are merged into the outbound generateContent request
over any client-sent labels, with the operator's value winning on key
conflicts so a caller cannot override the gateway's attribution. Label
keys and static values are validated against Google Cloud's label
requirements at config load; expressions that fail to produce a valid
value at request time reject the request (fail closed), so no request is
forwarded to Vertex unlabeled. Configs without `labels` are unchanged.

This gives operators the same invoice-grade attribution on Vertex that
session tags already give on Bedrock: the App/Team/tenant value on the
Vertex bill is set by the operator, not trusted from the caller.

Signed-off-by: Lyqed <antondoeswonders@gmail.com>
